{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Who will console you.</b> [It means] \"console,\" as in לנוד לו ולנחמו (Job 2:11)." "<b>השוד והשבר.</b> The שוד is the sword, for שוד is always with the sword, and the שבר is famine, as in בשברי לכם מטה לחם (Leviticus 26:26). And some say: the evils came in pairs." "<b>How shall I comfort you.</b> [There is] a missing bet in מי אנחמך, for a person is consoled when one tells him that what befell you already befell so-and-so likewise."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 51, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:05.056881967Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}